    Cheryl Ahmadi (KLVN Channel 4): Good evening, Las Vegas. I'm Cheryl Ahmadi.
    Cheryl Ahmadi (KLVN Channel 4): Local police are addressing growing concern over a rise in missing persons reports centered around the Strip. 
    Cheryl Ahmadi (KLVN Channel 4): The Clark County Sheriff's Department suggests that many of the individuals may have come to Las Vegas seeking a fresh start.
    Cheryl Ahmadi (KLVN Channel 4): Still, some residents are voicing unease, citing unfamiliar faces and fringe groups active in the area.
    Cheryl Ahmadi (KLVN Channel 4): LVMPD advises the public to exercise common sense, remain in well-lit spaces, and avoid individuals of what they describe as 'of a Satanic and/or communist persuasion.'
    Cheryl Ahmadi (KLVN Channel 4): This is Cheryl Ahmadi, KLVN Channel 4. We'll be back after the break.
